{"id": "EUVD-2026-72455", "enisaUuid": "dfef33c0-945c-35a9-a473-1dc35e9ec2c8", "description": "A heap buffer overflow flaw was found in the SASL I/O layer of 389 Directory Server (389-ds-base). In sasl_io_start_packet(), the wrapped-record length read from the wire is validated only against an upper bound. A small wire length (0, 1, or 2) produces an encrypted_buffer_count below the already-consumed encrypted_buffer_offset, causing an unsigned subtraction underflow in sasl_io_read_packet(). PR_Recv is then requested to read approximately 4 GiB into a 1024-byte heap buffer, resulting in a heap buffer overflow with attacker-controlled content. After a successful SASL bind with integrity protection (SSF > 0), a remote authenticated attacker can cause a denial of service or potentially achieve remote code execution. This flaw is distinct from CVE-2026-11774, whose fix only guards against upper-bound overflow.", "datePublished": "2026-09-07T14:14:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-08T14:14:49", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:64771", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:64776", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:64778", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:64779", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:64780", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:64781", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:64783", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:64784", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:64785", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:64789", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:64790", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:64791", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:64792", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:64793", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:64804", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:65119", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:79217", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-18355", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2509186"], "aliases": ["GHSA-r5vv-79fp-2427", "CVE-2026-18355"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.84, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0d34e2f6-98f2-3f29-bfa5-50a02685d537", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8.8 Telecommunications Update Service", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 8080020260831180218.6dbb3803"}, {"id": "0f609f29-6a3c-3015-b1ca-856112aaf87b", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9.2 Update Services for SAP Solutions", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:2.2.4-22.el9_2"}, {"id": "10be86fc-3378-3a14-bc19-c3c032141d29", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Directory Server 11.7 E4S for RHEL 8", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 8080020260903102346.f969626e"}, {"id": "2f23fcc5-7782-370a-b783-421f084f533f", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9.6 Extended Update Support", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:2.6.1-24.el9_6"}, {"id": "345188e3-9a1b-315a-aa25-2df82d0a329b", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Directory Server 12.2 E4S for RHEL 9", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 9020020260903155914.1674d574"}, {"id": "35d4bb6a-ee4c-37fd-9fac-32ad53818a0f", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 8100020260904155442.25e700aa"}, {"id": "3cc6fea8-13c9-362b-ad82-448ec46f50ec", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Directory Server 12.4 E4S for RHEL 9", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 9040020260903102623.1674d574"}, {"id": "40482d30-2984-3c9c-8723-54df295488c3", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Directory Server 11.5 E4S for RHEL 8", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 8060020260908152739.0ca98e7e"}, {"id": "4c35d0ac-6fa1-3127-b021-b13e2230c8b3", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9", "vendor": {"name": "R